  "frame_key": "85164605|1|decision|41",
  "note": "85164605 f41 (Main, mega_starmie seat 1, turn 5). Hand 8 holds BOTH Mega Signal (Item: search deck for a Mega Evolution Pokemon ex) and Salvatore (Supporter: evolve one of my Pokemon straight from deck) -- either reaches the same board, a second Mega Starmie ex. Board: Cinderace Active 120/160 with 1{W} and retreat 0; benched Staryu with 3{W}; benched Staryu with none. The turn converges on the same 2-prize double-KO regardless of first action: evolve a Staryu -> Mega Starmie ex, free-retreat Cinderace into the charged body, Jetting Blow 120 KOs Kadabra (80 HP) and its 50 bench rider exactly KOs an Abra (50 HP). correct=[3] Mega Signal -- spend the Item, keep the Supporter slot.",
  "claims": {
    "decision": {
      "correct": [
        3
      ],
      "owner": "#145",
      "ruled": "2026-07-27",
      "why": "HELD OUT as a NEAR-INDIFFERENT turn whose residual is a readiness-currency question, not a #175 one. User ruling 2026-07-27: the correction is valid (Item before Supporter) but immaterial HERE -- 'since we will not play a supporter this turn otherwise, it doesn't really matter'. The leaf agrees and always did: NINE of eleven options tie at exactly 2207.50 pre-change (correct_is_unique_top False), because every one of them reaches the same 2-prize double-KO. The correct option's value is IDENTICAL before and after #175 (2207.50); what moved is a sibling. Ties break by option order, so the leaf's real pick was index 0 (Salvatore) both before and after -- the committed action is wrong identically either way, and the flip is a metric artifact of the lenient shared-max rule, not a behaviour regression. What #175 actually changed, traced at e1fbb8d vs aefc1c7: inside the Lillie's branch the sim stopped paying Ultra Ball's cost with two {W} Energy and instead discarded a Pokegear, attaching the saved Energy to the benched Staryu -- strictly better play, readiness 157.5 -> 172.08, same 2 prizes, same survival. That surfaced the real question, which is #145's: `_readiness` ranks a benched Staryu carrying 1{W} (172.08) ABOVE a benched second Mega Starmie ex with none (157.5). That is the leaf's own currency calibration -- #145 owns `_readiness` (planner.py:3119) and the currency audit. Corpus-wide the change is neutral-to-positive: strict correctness 34 -> 35, avg_top_tie 3.112 -> 3.086."
